        <m>0</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>\mathbf{v}=3 \mathbf{i} + \mathbf{j} + \mathbf{k}</m> and use the distributive law:



<m>\mathbf{v}\times\mathbf{i} = \left( 3 \mathbf{i} + \mathbf{j} + \mathbf{k} \right) \times \mathbf{i} = 
3 \mathbf{i} \times \mathbf{i} +  \mathbf{j}\times \mathbf{i} +  \mathbf{k} \times \mathbf{i} = 3 \cdot\mathbf{ 0} -  \mathbf{k} +  \mathbf{j} = 
\left\lt  \begin{array}{ccc} 0, \amp  1, \amp  -1  \end{array} \right&gt;</m>



<m>\mathbf{v}\times\mathbf{j} = \left( 3 \mathbf{i} + \mathbf{j} + \mathbf{k} \right) \times \mathbf{j} = 
3 \mathbf{i} \times \mathbf{j} +  \mathbf{j}\times \mathbf{j} +  \mathbf{k} \times \mathbf{j} = 3 \mathbf{k} + 1 \cdot \mathbf{ 0} -  \mathbf{i} = 
\left\lt  \begin{array}{ccc} -1, \amp  0, \amp  3  \end{array} \right&gt;</m>



<m>\mathbf{v}\times\mathbf{k} = \left( 3 \mathbf{i} + \mathbf{j} + \mathbf{k} \right) \times \mathbf{k} = 
3 \mathbf{i} \times \mathbf{k} +  \mathbf{j}\times \mathbf{k} +  \mathbf{k} \times \mathbf{k} = -3 \mathbf{j} +  \mathbf{i} - 1 \cdot \mathbf{ 0} = 
\left\lt  \begin{array}{ccc} 1, \amp  -3, \amp  0  \end{array} \right&gt;</m>



</solution>
